{"id": "q_battle_with_the_wolf_and_aftermath_1", "question": "When the council-chamber fight ends, where does that leave the Wolf-dead, fled, what?", "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf ends the council-chamber fight dead—“Decapitated; head removed from body;”—with Bonogo taking the head, overriding earlier escape attempts.\n\nThere is a conflict in OBSERVED facts:  \n- The Wolf’s operational_status includes escape behavior (invisible, fleeing via secret passage).  \n- However, later OBSERVED facts show a terminal outcome: “Decapitated; head removed from body;” and Bonogo explicitly “Removed the Wolf’s head to transport it.”\n\nBecause terminal outcomes take precedence and represent the final state in play, the current, authoritative outcome is that the Wolf is dead, not fled.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- physical_condition: “Decapitated; head removed from body;”; previously invisible and damaged  \n- operational_status: Earlier attempted escape via invisibility and secret passage, but superseded by death  \n- location: Council Room (scene of confrontation)  \n- role: Central adversary in the council chamber battle  \n- faction: cultist\n\nSo when the fight ends, the Wolf is conclusively dead, with his body destroyed and head in Bonogo’s possession.", "has_error": false, "retrieval": {"enabled": true, "top_k": 30, "pre_filter_count": 732, "post_filter_count": 30, "duration_ms": 28485, "top_5": [["ent_arcane_locks", 1.8], ["ent_the_wolf", 1.791], ["ent_branching_paths_after_the_fight", 1.7273], ["ent_magic_pulse_alarms", 1.689], ["ent_battle_with_the_wolf_in_the_council_chamber", 1.6]], "selected_entity_ids": ["ent_arcane_locks", "ent_the_wolf", "ent_branching_paths_after_the_fight", "ent_magic_pulse_alarms", "ent_battle_with_the_wolf_in_the_council_chamber", "ent_doors_lock_magically", "ent_speak_with_dead", "ent_escape_tunnel", "ent_dead_horse", "ent_citizenry", "ent_magical_alarm_system", "ent_fight", "ent_city_council", "ent_corrupted_guard_patrol", "ent_thalia", "ent_the_city",