{"id": "q_battle_with_the_wolf_and_aftermath_2", "question": "What does the council room itself throw at us that screws with the fight?", "answer": "TL;DR: The council chamber fights back with arcane traps, illusions, and environmental hazards—especially targeting anyone without amulets—causing paralysis, force damage, disorientation, and falling debris.\n\nThe room itself is actively hostile:\n\n- CANON: Arcane defenses are keyed to amulets—**Players (group)** without them “may be targeted by traps,” while **Guards** are “exempt…via amulets.”\n- OBSERVED: These traps manifest as **arcane trap bursts** that “can temporarily paralyze” and deal “2d6 force damage.”\n- OBSERVED: The space is unstable—players are “forced to dodge falling debris hazards.”\n- CANON/OBSERVED: Illusion effects are in play—players are “disoriented by the illusory walls/illusion spells,” compounding battlefield confusion.\n- OBSERVED: **Rune alarms** are active, escalating the fight by alerting enemies and locking things down.\n- CANON: The chamber ties into the city’s machinery—shifts in the **wall hum** can signal changes or trigger effects mid-fight.\n\nNet effect: the room punishes positioning, awareness, and gear (amulets), while scrambling player perception and layering damage + control effects.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Arcane traps keyed to amulets; rune alarms\n- Hazards: Falling debris; force-damage bursts; paralysis\n- Environmental Effects: Illusory walls; disorientation; shifting wall hum signals", "has_error": false, "retrieval": {"enabled": true, "top_k": 30, "pre_filter_count": 732, "post_filter_count": 30, "duration_ms": 31559, "top_5": [["ent_flesh_golem", 2.0343], ["ent_the_city", 1.84], ["ent_council_room", 1.8139], ["ent_city_council", 1.8064], ["ent_falling_debris", 1.7191]], "selected_entity_ids": ["ent_flesh_golem", "ent_the_city", "ent_council_room", "ent_city_council", "ent_falling_debris", "ent_side_chambers", "ent_exodus_from_the_lundayell_empire", "ent_citys_