{"id": "q_arch_current", "question": "What does the Council Room look like after the wolf fight-what should we notice?", "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Room shows clear signs of a chaotic fight—most notably the Wolf’s corpse (decapitated; head removed from body) and multiple guards showing corruption with an oily sheen in their eyes, creating an atmosphere of tension and mistrust.\n\nWhat you should notice:\n\n- The Wolf (OBSERVED): His body is present and unmistakably defeated—**Decapitated; head removed from body**. This is the clearest proof of the confrontation’s outcome and his betrayal.\n- Guards (OBSERVED): Several guards display **an oily sheen to their eyes**, signaling corruption. Their behavior is tense and unstable, reinforcing that the threat isn’t over.\n- Guard positioning (OBSERVED): Guards had been **placed in a ring along the wall**, suggesting a defensive or containment posture during the incident.\n- Atmosphere (OBSERVED): The guards are **visibly tense, some in disbelief**, indicating the fight has shaken confidence and control within the chamber.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Physical Condition: Wolf decapitated; guards show oily-eyed corruption  \n- Defenses/State: Guards on alert, tense, and maintaining order  \n- Scene Tone: Aftermath of betrayal, confusion, and lingering internal threat", "has_error": false, "retrieval": {"enabled": true, "top_k": 30, "pre_filter_count": 732, "post_filter_count": 30, "duration_ms": 35231, "top_5": [["ent_branching_paths_after_the_fight", 1.9794], ["ent_corrupted_meat", 1.92], ["ent_the_wolf", 1.8988], ["ent_illusion_spells", 1.8093], ["ent_council_room", 1.7435]], "selected_entity_ids": ["ent_branching_paths_after_the_fight", "ent_corrupted_meat", "ent_the_wolf", "ent_illusion_spells", "ent_council_room", "ent_meat_piles", "ent_the_city", "ent_arcane_locks", "ent_magical_alarm_system", "ent_statues", "ent_tapestries", "ent_gnome", "ent_battle_with_the_wolf_in_the_council_chamber", "ent_political_intrigue_among_the_c