{"id": "q_arch_delta", "question": "What got wrecked or changed in the Council Room during Session 12?", "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Chambers were heavily disrupted—lit up by a Fireball, magically activated (runes and illusions), and left generally disheveled.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Physical Condition (OBSERVED): The room is described as “Disheveled,” indicating clear aftermath damage or disorder.\n- Atmosphere (OBSERVED): “almost the entire room is lit up by Fireball,” showing significant destructive or at least chaotic magical impact during the session.\n- Defenses (OBSERVED): Runes along the walls activated when Caelynn cast her spell, and Illusory Walls were present/engaged—meaning the chamber’s magical defenses were actively triggered and altered the environment mid-scene.\n- Geography (OBSERVED): No structural changes explicitly stated, but the presence of a hidden trapdoor and large central table may have been affected indirectly (not confirmed as damaged).\n\nOverall, Session 12 turned the Council Room from a formal deliberation space into an active, magically volatile battlefield environment, with both visible disorder and triggered defensive systems.", "has_error": false, "retrieval": {"enabled": true, "top_k": 30, "pre_filter_count": 732, "post_filter_count": 30, "duration_ms": 43894, "top_5": [["ent_players", 2.0], ["ent_city_council", 1.7451], ["ent_council_room", 1.6848], ["ent_side_chambers", 1.4848], ["ent_exodus_from_the_lundayell_empire", 1.4848]], "selected_entity_ids": ["ent_players", "ent_city_council", "ent_council_room", "ent_side_chambers", "ent_exodus_from_the_lundayell_empire", "ent_citys_rise_to_prominence", "ent_council_headquarters", "ent_soft_shifting_lights", "ent_tapestries", "ent_healing_potions", "ent_professor_tealeaf", "ent_small_dais", "ent_political_intrigue_among_the_council", "ent_gnome", "ent_karsemine_the_tiefling_ranger", "ent_statues", "ent_battle_with_the_wolf_in_the_council_chamber", "ent_corrupted_meat", "ent_the_crew"